  "name": "Old Regular Baptist lined hymnody (southeastern Kentucky)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Unaccompanied congregational hymn singing of the Old Regular Baptists, a conservative Baptist association of the central Appalachian coalfields of eastern Kentucky, southwestern Virginia and southern West Virginia that uses no instruments in worship. A song leader chants each line of a hymn from a words-only hymnbook and the congregation follows in slow, free-flowing unison, each singer adding personal ornaments so that the voices overlap in a dense heterophony; Smithsonian Folkways issued recordings made among the Indian Bottom Association of Letcher County and neighbouring congregations in 1997.",
